Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Finding a Contraction Path", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"802b4dc6-b3ed-4f96-99ee-c1eb5a531ef1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The cost of contracting a network depends drastically on the order in which \
pairs are merged. A path is a list of pairs {i, j} using the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["OptimalContractionPath",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/OptimalContractionPath"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"60d8c4f4-64b1-4d7d-8039-bfc5a1d2d45f"],
 " convention: at each step the tensors in positions i and j are contracted, \
both are removed, and the result is appended to the end of the list. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["OptimalContractionPath",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/OptimalContractionPath"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8c674d7e-901d-4fad-a2f1-72d6baadacdb"],
 " runs a full search; with Method \[Rule] \"flops\" it minimizes the total \
floating-point operation count rather than the default \"size\" objective:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"61620943-cebf-44d5-9312-c9dbe0cf0ba9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"path", "=", 
  RowBox[{"OptimalContractionPath", "[", 
   RowBox[{"mps", ",", 
    RowBox[{"Method", "\[Rule]", "\"\<flops\>\""}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",Expres\
sionUUID->"32fce00c-9275-4f79-8f54-9b6336ffbca5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Exhaustive search becomes infeasible once the network grows beyond about a \
dozen tensors. For larger problems, reach for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["GreedyContractionPath",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/GreedyContractionPath"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f43f0339-917b-4d6f-acc5-f6c3beb94458"],
 ", which picks the locally cheapest pair at every step:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"81330e8a-c6d7-4379-9f0f-83498a296896"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"GreedyContractionPath", "[", "mps", "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"332640ca-e296-4c01-9e82-af6cb41c3453"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If you do not supply a path explicitly, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetworkContract",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetworkContract"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"db9c12e6-3424-4f73-8d68-28805c13560d"],
 " calls a planner of its own and uses the result. Passing an explicit path \
matters when you want reproducibility across runs, when the heuristic and the \
optimum diverge, or when you wish to time the search separately from the \
execution."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02ed2d5c-f991-40b9-9608-a2fddafa8f3c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Contracting", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"88c8ba32-b673-4560-b62a-586d9219b351"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Once a path is fixed, execution is one call. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetworkContract",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetworkContract"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"d73c5291-3bda-4848-8fc1-4765f925a8ba"],
 " carries out every pairwise contraction in order and returns a numerical \
array whose free indices match those of the input network:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8e1c39b8-b4b9-41ed-90b3-68977665aa72"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"result", "=", 
  RowBox[{"TensorNetworkContract", "[", "mps", "]"}]}]], "Input",ExpressionUUI\
D->"b75c025b-86c3-4a2a-86f2-12c3df75bf2b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The shape is informative: six dangling indices, each of physical dimension \
2, give a rank-6 array which is the unnormalized state vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["s", "1"], " ", 
     SubscriptBox["s", "2"], " ", 
     SubscriptBox["s", "3"], " ", 
     SubscriptBox["s", "4"], " ", 
     SubscriptBox["s", "5"], " ", 
     SubscriptBox["s", "6"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"bc92976b-021b-482b-8908-394fd60245ca"],
 " of the spin chain encoded by the MPS:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"20391ddc-4134-43b2-856c-42c730cac45f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "result", "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dd3fa4f6-7b1f-4535-8f6e-688e3678c5fd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two siblings of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetworkContract",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetworkContract"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"ac621621-70e8-4e31-81e3-9478fbc11225"],
 " are worth knowing. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetworkContraction",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetworkContraction"]],
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"59d6ea56-3222-463c-a5df-4f88f06ff299"],
 " returns an Inactive symbolic expression representing the planned \
contraction \[Dash] handy for inspecting which sub-tensors will be built and \
in what order. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ActivateTensors",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ActivateTensors"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0ed40c19-66fc-4da5-839f-1f1211df87a7"],
 " then evaluates that expression. The available execution back-ends are \
listed in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["$TensorNetworkContractionMethods",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->
    "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/$TensorNetworkContractionMethods"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"74771dbb-8873-42e0-8028-e8a92a15b690"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3118a5fc-ffe4-4594-9cb7-7a918412af45"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Where to Go Next", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"85d0c3a5-941f-4e52-bfde-71f912357da2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Five sibling tutorials drill into the tiers sketched above. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox[
   RowBox[{"Building", " ", "Tensor", " ", "Networks"}],
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->
    "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/tutorial/BuildingTensorNetworks"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"fbe38b7e-0bec-404d-9073-e7fc5e5beefd"],
 " catalogs the constructors \\[Dash] PEPS, MERA, tree tensor networks, \
transforms like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["BinaryTensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/BinaryTensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b6763627-69c6-4d04-9f48-6730a3e44c42"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["SparseTensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/SparseTensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1f0f2bab-75e9-4d9d-aef3-bd04b3e84672"],
 ", and graph adapters via ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ToTensorNetworkGraph",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ToTensorNetworkGraph"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"74d9f2e1-8e8b-41b8-b2d0-13ae1128218c"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox[
   RowBox[{"Contraction", " ", "Paths", " ", "and", " ", "Execution"}],
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->
    "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/tutorial/ContractionPathsAndExecution"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"9dc3b02e-d20e-4192-bf22-1bbd3c19405e"],
 " surveys the planner objectives (\"size\", \"flops\", \"max\", \"write\", \
\"combo\", \"limit\"), the path utilities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["PathQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/PathQ"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"828b4795-bdc5-4200-9a0a-ef22ddd71cb7"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CanonicalPath",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/CanonicalPath"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"cea9b3f1-7aa3-4e26-bd3b-cac5cb08be3d"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ContractionTree",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ContractionTree"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"dd8a59af-ca3c-453f-9223-90a62aa3a376"],
 ", and the execution back-ends. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox[
   RowBox[{"Matrix", " ", "Product", " ", "States"}],
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/tutorial/MPSAlgorithms"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"df09b61a-4d58-4c18-8e49-52640e72583d"],
 " treats the algorithmic toolkit attached to one-dimensional networks. The \
two subpackage tutorials cover the named-index layer \\[Dash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox[
   RowBox[{"Named", " ", "Indices", " ", "and", " ", "Metrics"}],
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->
    "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/tutorial/IndexArrayAndMetrics"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"72008d22-1298-4832-a493-3bb867eafea1"],
 " \\[Dash] and the representation theory of permutation symmetry of tensors \
via ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox[
   RowBox[{
   "Young", " ", "Tableaux", " ", "and", " ", "Tensor", " ", "Symmetries"}],
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/tutorial/YoungSymmetries"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"9ca366bf-a33d-4a04-bb22-a1901b2b6c87"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d6e44f0f-3fea-474e-a308-de2191ba93a6"]
}, Open  ]],

